    "executiveSummary": "Human cognition conserves metabolic energy by carving recurring decisions into automated subroutines deep inside the basal ganglia. Like a driver navigating an empty freeway on muscle memory, an operator runs on automated scripts until an explicit signal demands manual intervention. When you fail to audit these underlying scripts, you surrender operational control to legacy patterns that erode margin, discipline, and competitive advantage.\n\nAt the institutional scale, organizations operate as networks of informal truces and shared habits rather than rational spreadsheets. Just as water carves physical channels into rock, daily corporate routines dictate how safety issues, customer friction, and strategic pivots are handled under pressure. Elite leadership identifies 'keystone habits'\u2014high-leverage behavioral pivot points where a single enforced routine forces discipline through an entire supply chain or culture.\n\nRewiring behavior does not require brute willpower; it demands mechanical precision. By preserving the existing cue and reward while substituting the central routine, individuals and enterprises execute systematic behavioral upgrades with near-zero friction. Habits are not immutable destiny; they are structural architecture waiting to be redesigned.",
